   "html_text": "While associating collectives with moral blameworthiness is difficult, it is not, as we have seen, impossible. Indeed, by both reimagining moral blameworthiness in the context of groups and developing alternative notions of collective agency that allow us to locate such moral blameworthiness, we can move toward a coherent and empirically feasible practice of collective moral responsibility. Two recent efforts to defend collective moral responsibility appear to be particularly promising in this c",
